course: dictionary
lesson: 12986
title: Expenditure: money and energy spent
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Expenditure is a formal word that you will meet in maths, business and science. It means the amount of something that has been used up, and most often it is money.
explain: «The club's expenditure was 300 dollars.» Here expenditure is the total money the club spent. If the club spent 300 dollars, then 300 dollars went out.
explain: Expenditure can also mean using up energy, time or effort. In science, «energy expenditure» is how much energy your body uses up, such as when you run.
fact: Expenditure means the total amount of money spent.
fact: Expenditure can also mean using up energy, time or effort.
fact: Useful phrases are «total expenditure» and «expenditure on», as in «expenditure on books».
fact: In a budget, income minus expenditure is what is left over.
fact: Expenditure is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in school, business and science, not in everyday chat.
exercise: «The club's expenditure was 300 dollars.» What does expenditure mean here? | The number of club members | *The money the club spent | A place where people play sport | The money the club earned
exercise: In a budget, what is income minus expenditure? | The money from sales | The total money spent | *What is left over | A loan from the bank
exercise: «Running fast needs a high energy expenditure.» What does energy expenditure mean? | Carrying heavy bags | *Using up a lot of energy | Having no energy at all | Gaining energy from sleep
test: «The school's expenditure on new books was 500 pounds.» What is the expenditure here? | The number of new books | The money the school earned from books | *The total money spent on new books | A list of books to borrow
test: Which phrase means using up time or effort? | A map of the town | A profit from the shop | *An expenditure of time on the project | A bank account with savings
exam: Which phrase means the total amount of money spent? | total income | *total expenditure | total guess | total distance
